# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS HERE (it is not just style):
#
# scripts/bump-cache.js computes the ?v= cache-bust token as a SHA-1 of each
# asset's raw bytes on disk. With core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, a
# Windows clone checks every file out as CRLF while the committed blob is LF —
# so the same file hashes differently on Windows than on the Linux host that
# actually serves it.
#
# The practical consequence: running `npm run prep-deploy` on Windows rewrote
# every ?v= token to a CRLF-derived hash that never matches the LF bytes
# Hostinger serves, and `--check` reported all 7 HTML files permanently stale.
# Pinning eol=lf makes the hash identical on every machine.
#
# Do not remove this file without also reworking bump-cache.js to normalise
# line endings before hashing.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the asset types bump-cache.js hashes.
*.js   text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.php  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.xml  text eol=lf
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF or they fail on the server with a bad-interpreter
# error — scripts/ensure-uploads-symlink.sh runs from cron on Hostinger.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
